The `-Origin` parameter for `Submit-SigningRequest` is a hashtable that provides information about the origin of the artifact. It is available for Pipeline Integrity and Open Source Code Signing and should only be used from a Trusted Build System.

The keys in the `-Origin` hashtable can include nested hashtables such as:

- `RepositoryData` with keys:
  - `SourceControlManagementType` (e.g., "svn")
  - `Url` (e.g., repository URL)
  - `BranchName` (e.g., branch name)
  - `CommitId` (e.g., commit hash)

- `BuildData` with keys:
  - `Url` (e.g., build URL)
  - `BuildSettingsFile` (e.g., path to build settings file)

Example usage:

```powershell
-Origin @{
    RepositoryData=@{
        SourceControlManagementType="svn";
        Url="https://github.com/org/project";
        BranchName="release/v2.1";
        CommitId="bf458b27080c81eb1e316c63867a87fdb3b47211"
    };
    BuildData=@{
        Url="https://ci.appveyor.com/project/org/name/builds/buildid/job/jobid";
        BuildSettingsFile="@settings.json"
    }
}
```

This example shows the structure and keys that can be used in the `-Origin` hashtable when submitting a signing request from a trusted build system [1][2][4].

**Sources:** [1] [PowerShell cmdlets > Submit-SigningRequest > Parameters > Parameters with -InputArtifactPath or -ArtifactRetrievalLink](https://docs.signpath.io/powershell/Submit-SigningRequest#parameters-with--inputartifactpath-or--artifactretrievallink) · [2] [PowerShell cmdlets > Submit-SigningRequest > Parameters > Parameters with -InputArtifactPath or -ArtifactRetrievalLink > Values for -Origin parameter](https://docs.signpath.io/powershell/Submit-SigningRequest#values-for--origin-parameter) · [4] [PowerShell cmdlets > Submit-SigningRequest > Examples > Example 5: Provide user-defined parameters and origin verification](https://docs.signpath.io/powershell/Submit-SigningRequest#example-params-origin)
